0249: count encoded passes, commands and draws per frame in the GPU profile

The AURORA_GPU_PROFILE text line reported GPU ms per pass and a per-frame "xN" count per pass, but no
totals, so a change that removed passes or draws had no number to prove it. The line ends with
", passes/frame N, commands/frame N, draws/frame N", accumulated only while the text profile is on:
counts_enabled() is one predictable branch per encoded GX pass otherwise, and the per-pass command
walk only runs inside it. The pass is encoded exactly as before; only counters are incremented.

--- a/lib/webgpu/gpu_prof.hpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/gpu_prof.hpp
@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@
 void frame_begin(const wgpu::CommandEncoder& encoder);
 void frame_end(const wgpu::CommandEncoder& encoder);
 void after_submit();
+// 0249: counts for a frame's encoded GX passes, commands and draws, printed by the AURORA_GPU_PROFILE
+// text line, so a change in passes/draws per frame can be proven. Free with the text profile off.
+bool counts_enabled();
+void note_encoded_pass(uint32_t commands, uint32_t draws);
 const wgpu::PassTimestampWrites* pass_writes(std::string_view name);
 
